## Rolling Polyhedral Dice

Tabletop RPGs use dice with different numbers of sides. A D4 is a pyramid with 4 sides. A D20 is the iconic 20-sided die.

### The Dice Enum

```xiom
enum Dice {
  D4,
  D6,
  D8,
  D10,
  D12,
  D20,
}
```

### Maximum Value Per Die

Each die type has a different maximum:

```xiom
fn Dice.max_value(self) -> Int {
  match self {
    D4 => { return 4; }
    D6 => { return 6; }
    D8 => { return 8; }
    D10 => { return 10; }
    D12 => { return 12; }
    D20 => { return 20; }
  }
}
```

### Simulating a Roll

A standalone function simulates a random roll for any die:

```xiom
fn roll(d: Dice) -> Int {
  let max = d.max_value();
  return (max / 2) + 1;
}
```

This uses a deterministic formula. For true randomness, check the `math` module.

### Rolling Multiple Times

```xiom
let d20 = Dice.D20;
roll(d20);  // e.g., 11
roll(d20);  // e.g., 11
roll(d20);  // e.g., 11

let d6 = Dice.D6;
roll(d6);   // e.g., 4
```

### Critical Hits

A D20 roll of 20 is a "critical hit" in many games:

```xiom
fn is_critical(d: Dice, result: Int) -> Bool {
  return d == Dice.D20 && result == 20;
}
```

